lso have a variety of smoothies, nachos, sandwiches, and candies. Snowballs are really reasonably priced and they do a solid job - plenty of syrup. Totally solid and as a local certainly recommend. Also open year round!"},{"business_id":"YSGxbx26Kouq-c4Ttz3FZA","review_id":"qB-WXaQxhoNIEXQUNNDESw","date":"2021-10-07T20:55:49","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.8961950540542603,"text_excerpt":"The best snowballs in New Orleans. I am obsessed with the Ice cream n cream/Nectar cream side by side. I literally will go there as soon as I get off the plane The staff is soooooo friendly and everyone love this place."},{"business_id":"YSGxbx26Kouq-c4Ttz3FZA","review_id":"ZvTgsK-gsDTu5nSkWi8wUw","date":"2015-05-10T01:53:19","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.8931806683540344,"text_excerpt":"My favorite snoball stand. This place has been a Gentilly institution for years. Nice small parking lot on the side, clean, friendly staff. It's usually pretty crowded but sometimes you get lucky at a slow time. They have lots of food choices but I've only ever had their snoballs. Prices are good --$2.50 per large. For .50 cents, you can grab a small bowl of shaved ice for your dog."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"YSGxbx26Kouq-c4Ttz3FZA","photo_id":"RpFZTa2zn3kK_gw8RPjKgw","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/RpFZTa2zn3kK_gw8RPjKgw.jpg","visual_representativeness":1.0}]},"notebook_case":null}
